{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GQeWGRqz2KQD4yS6HUc3Hm","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Prerender one page per public note (s/<slug>) and per author with a public note (a/<handle>).\nusage: build_pages.py content/stories.json .build/pages\"\"\"\nimport html, json, os, sys\n\nsrc, out = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]\nstories = [s for s in json.load(open(src)) if s.get(\"visibility\", \"public\") == \"public\"]\n\ndef page(title, body):\n    return (f\"<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=utf-8><title>{html.escape(title)} · fieldnotes</title>\"\n            f\"<link rel=stylesheet href=/style.css></head><body>{body}<script src=/app.js></script></body></html>\\n\")\n\ndef write(key, text):\n    p = os.path.join(out, key)\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(p, \"w\") as f:\n        f.write(text)\n\nauthors = {}\nfor s in stories:\n    write(f\"s/{s['slug']}\", page(s[\"title\"], f\"<h1>{html.escape(s['title'])}</h1><p>{html.escape(s['summary'])}</p>\"\n                                 f\"<p>by <a href=/a/{s['author']}>{s['author']}</a></p>\"))\n    authors.setdefault(s[\"author\"], []).append(s)\nfor handle, mine in authors.items():\n    items = \"\".join(f\"<li><a href=/s/{s['slug']}>{html.escape(s['title'])}</a></li>\" for s in mine)\n    write(f\"a/{handle}\", page(handle, f\"<h1>{handle}</h1><ul>{items}</ul>\"))\nprint(f\"  {len(stories)} notes, {len(authors)} authors\")\n---README\n# fieldnotes\n\nA static site for short field notes. The site itself is plain files in `site/`\n(the shell page, styles, script, robots.txt). Every note and every author also\ngets a prerendered page, so it can be shared and indexed: `build_pages.py`\nreads `content/stories.json` and writes `.build/pages/s/<slug>` and\n`.build/pages/a/<handle>`. Private notes get no page.\n\nThe site is served from an S3 bucket behind CloudFront. `deploy.sh` builds the\npages, syncs `site/` to the bucket and uploads the pages. The page keys have no\nfile extension (`s/<slug>`, not `s/<slug>.html`), so S3 cannot guess their\ntype: each one is uploaded with `--content-type \"text/html; charset=utf-8\"`,\notherwise browsers download the page instead of showing it.\n\nCI runs `./deploy.sh` on every push to main with `BUCKET` set and its own AWS\ncredentials. There is no test bucket.\n---GI\n.build/\n---STORIES\n[\n  {\"slug\": \"tide-tables-offline\", \"title\": \"Tide tables that work offline\", \"summary\": \"Caching a week of tide data on the phone before a trip.\", \"author\": \"ann\", \"visibility\": \"public\"},\n  {\"slug\": \"bird-calls-at-dawn\", \"title\": \"Recording bird calls at dawn\", \"summary\": \"Wind noise, gain and why the first ten minutes matter.\", \"author\": \"ann\", \"visibility\": \"public\"},\n  {\"slug\": \"trail-gpx-cleanup\", \"title\": \"Cleaning up a messy GPX track\", \"summary\": \"Dropping the points where the watch lost the signal.\", \"author\": \"bob\", \"visibility\": \"public\"},\n  {\"slug\": \"draft-moss-survey\", \"title\": \"Moss survey notes\", \"summary\": \"Not ready yet.\", \"author\": \"bob\", \"visibility\": \"private\"}\n]\n---APPJS\n// The shell page: lists the latest notes from /notes.json when it exists.\nfetch('/notes.json').then(r => r.ok ? r.json() : []).then(list => {\n  document.getElementById('app').innerHTML = list.map(n => `<p><a href=\"/s/${n.slug}\">${n.title}</a></p>`).join('');\n}).catch(() => {});\n---ROBOTS\nUser-agent: *\nAllow: /","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e50aedd-7681-48a5-8622-61657cc0c937","uuid":"ce22e90b-0b63-4bfc-bdb6-69acc091d4fd","timestamp":"2026-11-09T17:42:37.844Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Prerender one page per public note (s/<slug>) and per author with a public note (a/<handle>).\nusage: build_pages.py content/stories.json .build/pages\"\"\"\nimport html, json, os, sys\n\nsrc, out = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]\nstories = [s for s in json.load(open(src)) if s.get(\"visibility\", \"public\") == \"public\"]\n\ndef page(title, body):\n    return (f\"<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=utf-8><title>{html.escape(title)} · fieldnotes</title>\"\n            f\"<link rel=stylesheet href=/style.css></head><body>{body}<script src=/app.js></script></body></html>\\n\")\n\ndef write(key, text):\n    p = os.path.join(out, key)\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(p, \"w\") as f:\n        f.write(text)\n\nauthors = {}\nfor s in stories:\n    write(f\"s/{s['slug']}\", page(s[\"title\"], f\"<h1>{html.escape(s['title'])}</h1><p>{html.escape(s['summary'])}</p>\"\n                                 f\"<p>by <a href=/a/{s['author']}>{s['author']}</a></p>\"))\n    authors.setdefault(s[\"author\"], []).append(s)\nfor handle, mine in authors.items():\n    items = \"\".join(f\"<li><a href=/s/{s['slug']}>{html.escape(s['title'])}</a></li>\" for s in mine)\n    write(f\"a/{handle}\", page(handle, f\"<h1>{handle}</h1><ul>{items}</ul>\"))\nprint(f\"  {len(stories)} notes, {len(authors)} authors\")\n---README\n# fieldnotes\n\nA static site for short field notes. The site itself is plain files in `site/`\n(the shell page, styles, script, robots.txt). Every note and every author also\ngets a prerendered page, so it can be shared and indexed: `build_pages.py`\nreads `content/stories.json` and writes `.build/pages/s/<slug>` and\n`.build/pages/a/<handle>`. Private notes get no page.\n\nThe site is served from an S3 bucket behind CloudFront. `deploy.sh` builds the\npages, syncs `site/` to the bucket and uploads the pages. The page keys have no\nfile extension (`s/<slug>`, not `s/<slug>.html`), so S3 cannot guess their\ntype: each one is uploaded with `--content-type \"text/html; charset=utf-8\"`,\notherwise browsers download the page instead of showing it.\n\nCI runs `./deploy.sh` on every push to main with `BUCKET` set and its own AWS\ncredentials. There is no test bucket.\n---GI\n.build/\n---STORIES\n[\n  {\"slug\": \"tide-tables-offline\", \"title\": \"Tide tables that work offline\", \"summary\": \"Caching a week of tide data on the phone before a trip.\", \"author\": \"ann\", \"visibility\": \"public\"},\n  {\"slug\": \"bird-calls-at-dawn\", \"title\": \"Recording bird calls at dawn\", \"summary\": \"Wind noise, gain and why the first ten minutes matter.\", \"author\": \"ann\", \"visibility\": \"public\"},\n  {\"slug\": \"trail-gpx-cleanup\", \"title\": \"Cleaning up a messy GPX track\", \"summary\": \"Dropping the points where the watch lost the signal.\", \"author\": \"bob\", \"visibility\": \"public\"},\n  {\"slug\": \"draft-moss-survey\", \"title\": \"Moss survey notes\", \"summary\": \"Not ready yet.\", \"author\": \"bob\", \"visibility\": \"private\"}\n]\n---APPJS\n// The shell page: lists the latest notes from /notes.json when it exists.\nfetch('/notes.json').then(r => r.ok ? r.json() : []).then(list => {\n  document.getElementById('app').innerHTML = list.map(n => `<p><a href=\"/s/${n.slug}\">${n.title}</a></p>`).join('');\n}).catch(() => {});\n---ROBOTS\nUser-agent: *\nAllow: /","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GQeWGRqz2KQD4yS6HUc3Hm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
