{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsmTiN3PUB6uyb6fTuBd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is what I found:\n\n- `deploy.sh` has no `--delete` today, so stale site files and removed pages stay in the bucket.\n- Page keys are `s/<slug>` and `a/<handle>`, and they are only in `.build/pages`, not in `site/`.\n- Adding a plain `--delete` would reproduce the colleague's race: the sync would delete live pages before the upload restores them.\n\nMy approach is to pass every page key the build produces as an `--exclude` to the `--delete` sync. Stale pages and stale site files are then deleted by that one sync, and live pages are only overwritten in place. Bash 3.2 (macOS default) has no associative arrays, so I'll avoid them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1703,"cache_read_input_tokens":24184,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1703},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e50aedd-7681-48a5-8622-61657cc0c937","uuid":"c7cfe87f-3cd3-4d75-82d9-17ae2ba8b695","timestamp":"2026-11-09T17:43:03.896Z","request_id":"req_011CgsmTiAP2GvoJ7TMddbRi"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsmTiN3PUB6uyb6fTuBd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HRuyc9HZTF9qRZFu1jzXxs","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-K9wwLS/deploy.sh","old_string":"sync_site() {\n  echo \"→ syncing site/ to s3://$BUCKET\"\n  aws s3 sync \"$ROOT/site/\" \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --only-show-errors\n}\n\nupload_pages() {\n  # Page keys are extensionless (s/<slug>, a/<handle>), so S3 can't guess their\n  # type: upload each one with text/html.\n  echo \"→ uploading pages\"\n  ( cd \"$ROOT/.build/pages\" && find . -type f | sed 's|^\\./||' | sort | while read -r key; do\n      aws s3 cp \"$key\" \"s3://$BUCKET/$key\" --content-type \"text/html; charset=utf-8\" \\\n        --cache-control \"max-age=300\" --only-show-errors\n    done )\n}","new_string":"page_keys() {\n  ( cd \"$ROOT/.build/pages\" && find . -type f | sed 's|^\\./||' | sort )\n}\n\nsync_site() {\n  echo \"→ syncing site/ to s3://$BUCKET\"\n  # --delete removes everything in the bucket that this build no longer produces:\n  # removed site/ files and stale or unpublished pages. Pages this build does\n  # produce are excluded, so the sync never removes a live page; upload_pages\n  # overwrites them in place. (--exclude matches the exact key, no wildcards.)\n  local excludes=()\n  local key\n  while IFS= read -r key; do\n    excludes+=(--exclude \"$key\")\n  done < <(page_keys)\n  aws s3 sync \"$ROOT/site/\" \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete \\\n    ${excludes[@]+\"${excludes[@]}\"} --only-show-errors\n}\n\nupload_pages() {\n  # Page keys are extensionless (s/<slug>, a/<handle>), so S3 can't guess their\n  # type: upload each one with text/html. Each cp overwrites the old page in\n  # place, so the old version stays served until the new one replaces it.\n  echo \"→ uploading pages\"\n  ( cd \"$ROOT/.build/pages\" && page_keys | while read -r key; do\n      aws s3 cp \"$key\" \"s3://$BUCKET/$key\" --content-type \"text/html; charset=utf-8\" \\\n        --cache-control \"max-age=300\" --only-show-errors\n    done )\n}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1703,"cache_read_input_tokens":24184,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1703},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e50aedd-7681-48a5-8622-61657cc0c937","uuid":"15d88adf-5a00-47cc-be07-cfea3c9c235b","timestamp":"2026-11-09T17:43:06.451Z","request_id":"req_011CgsmTiAP2GvoJ7TMddbRi","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HRuyc9HZTF9qRZFu1jzXxs":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-K9wwLS/deploy.sh","old_string":"sync_site() {\n  echo \"→ syncing site/ to s3://$BUCKET\"\n  aws s3 sync \"$ROOT/site/\" \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --only-show-errors\n}\n\nupload_pages() {\n  # Page keys are extensionless (s/<slug>, a/<handle>), so S3 can't guess their\n  # type: upload each one with text/html.\n  echo \"→ uploading pages\"\n  ( cd \"$ROOT/.build/pages\" && find . -type f | sed 's|^\\./||' | sort | while read -r key; do\n      aws s3 cp \"$key\" \"s3://$BUCKET/$key\" --content-type \"text/html; charset=utf-8\" \\\n        --cache-control \"max-age=300\" --only-show-errors\n    done )\n}","new_string":"page_keys() {\n  ( cd \"$ROOT/.build/pages\" && find . -type f | sed 's|^\\./||' | sort )\n}\n\nsync_site() {\n  echo \"→ syncing site/ to s3://$BUCKET\"\n  # --delete removes everything in the bucket that this build no longer produces:\n  # removed site/ files and stale or unpublished pages. Pages this build does\n  # produce are excluded, so the sync never removes a live page; upload_pages\n  # overwrites them in place. (--exclude matches the exact key, no wildcards.)\n  local excludes=()\n  local key\n  while I