{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsmY5dpeEwNajo7XkaC5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed `deploy.sh` so each deploy removes anything in the bucket that the build no longer produces. The change is verified only with a stub `aws` CLI, not against a real bucket, so it needs one test deploy before you rely on it. I wrote the details in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**What changed**\n- The `site/` sync now runs with `--delete`. Deleted notes, private notes and removed `site/` files are cleaned up on the next deploy.\n- Every page the build produces is passed as an `--exclude` to that sync, so a live page is never deleted before the upload overwrites it. The exclude list comes from `.build/pages`, so it follows the build.\n- The upload loop still overwrites each page at the same key, so the old version stays up until the new one replaces it.\n- `build_pages` now creates its output folder. Without this, a site with zero public notes failed the deploy.\n\n**Colleague's note:** I used its diagnosis and its exclude-and-overwrite approach, and I used its verify idea (polling a story URL during a deploy). I did not add its separate stale-page cleanup step, because the main `--delete` sync already removes stale pages. I also did not hardcode prefixes, since this repo only produces `s/` and `a/`.\n\n**Testing:** `bash -n` passes. A dry run with a stub `aws` shows the expected commands, and the zero-notes case and missing `BUCKET` both behave. I did not deploy, so the live polling check is untested. I also could not confirm that `sync --delete` honors `--exclude` on real S3. That is documented CLI behavior, but the fix depends on it.\n\n**Risks:**\n- Any object in the bucket that this repo does not produce will be deleted on the first deploy. `site/app.js` fetches `/notes.json`, but nothing here creates it, so if another tool uploads it, it will be removed.\n- `--exclude` treats `*`, `?` and `[` as wildcards. A slug or handle with those characters would not be protected. I did not add a check for this."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2500,"cache_read_input_tokens":36224,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2500},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e50aedd-7681-48a5-8622-61657cc0c937","uuid":"6766b638-0e45-4ca1-af71-ca0feca56525","timestamp":"2026-11-09T17:43:42.287Z","request_id":"req_011CgsmY5JjLMtPNmT6UUyoh"}
